{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.5040346721316943, "attempt": 1, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. The change only uses K_test rows, which are similarities between test and training molecules. It fits one local SVR per test molecule on its 300 most similar training molecules, using training labels only. There is no file access and no use of test labels.", "No bug that would make the result meaningless. The indexing with np.ix_(idx, idx) and K_test[i:i+1, idx] is consistent. The rank-transformed, standardized target is reused the same way as in the incumbent. Runtime is about 2,900 small SVR fits per job, well within the time limit.", "Recomputed z: (0.4830 - 0.504) / (0.0070 * sqrt(1/1 + 1/1)) = -0.021 / 0.0099 = -2.12. This matches the harness value of -2.117; the small gap comes from 0.504 being rounded. Loss is lower-is-better, so the candidate is worse by about 0.021. Rejecting it is correct.", "Side note: the per-molecule loop makes the code more complex for a worse result, so the simplicity rule also argues against it."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Replace the single global SVR with a per-test-molecule local SVR: each test molecule gets a fresh SVR (C=5, epsilon=0.05) fit on its 300 most similar training molecules by the existing 0.5*(Tanimoto+RBF) kernel, using the same rank-normalized, standardized target.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b028", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_clear_HH_1_s1-candidate-14_1795049309725", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00187954, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00187954, "latency_s": 5.455338838044554, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7221, "tokens_out": 1397}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0250398, "cost_usd_