{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.48044884511565955, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No measurement circumvention: the change only swaps binary Morgan bits for count Morgan fingerprints and swaps Tanimoto for the MinMax (generalized Jaccard) kernel. No file access, no pasted answers, no test labels used.", "MinMax implementation looks correct: sum_k (A>=k)(B>=k)^T gives sum_i min(a_i, b_i), and na + nb - inter gives sum_i max(a_i, b_i) when na and nb are count sums. The tail of the function is unchanged and still computes inter/(na+nb-inter). The kernel stays positive semi-definite, so the downstream kernel method stays valid.", "Recomputed z: (0.4830-0.4804)/(0.0070*sqrt(2)) = 0.26. That matches the harness's 0.255 within rounding of the reported means.", "The gain of about 0.0026 is well under the noise sd of 0.0070, with n=1 on each side. 'Reject' is consistent with the numbers. A replicate would be needed to tell whether count/MinMax actually helps.", "Minor cost note: the loop runs up to the max count per bit, often 10-30+ iterations of n\u00d7n matmuls. That is fine at n\u2248970 but adds runtime compared with plain Tanimoto."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Switch Morgan featurization to radius-2 2048-bin count fingerprints and replace the binary Tanimoto kernel with a MinMax kernel, computed exactly via sum(min) = sum over count thresholds k of (count>=k) inner products, with sum(max) = sum(a)+sum(b)-sum(min); the descriptor RBF kernel, 0.5/0.5 mix, rank target and SVR are unchanged.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b044", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_clear_HH_1_s1-candidate-21_1795050232780", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00256234, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00256234, "latency_s": 11.100814778998028, "