{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.48243204141033846, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. The only change applies an inverse-normal (probit) transform to the rank-scaled training labels. It uses train_y only, and test labels are never touched.", "No bug. (rank-0.5)/n always lies strictly between 0 and 1, so norm.ppf returns finite values. The z-scoring that follows (mu, sd) still works. Predictions only need to be in the right order for Spearman, so the monotone transform does not need to be undone.", "The z value roughly checks out. The difference is 0.4830 - 0.4824 = 0.0006. With noise sd 0.0070 for each of the two single runs, the standard error is 0.0070*sqrt(2) = 0.0099, which gives z \u2248 0.061. The harness's 0.056 fits once you allow for rounding of the reported losses (a difference of about 0.00055).", "This gain is well below the noise level (one replicate each, about 0.09 sd). Rejecting is right, and the edit adds a little complexity for no measurable gain."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Replace the uniform rank target transform with a van der Waerden normal-score transform (norm.ppf of (rank-0.5)/n) before standardizing and fitting the SVR, leaving the kernel mix, C and epsilon unchanged.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b056", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_clear_HH_1_s1-candidate-29_1795051245238", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0015289400000000001, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0015289400000000001, "latency_s": 3.6151555340038612, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "coder", "served_model": "haiku", "tokens_in": 7208, "tokens_out": 701}, {"cost_usd_nominal": 0.0248198, "cost_usd_plan": 0.0248198, "latency_s": 9.308713874022942, "requested_model": "opus", "role":